## Context
Child of 1394. Stage 3 of the skill case notes pilot (`conception/2026-10-31-skill-case-notes.md` § 4). Stage 1 and the headless Claude read-back landed in PR #2114 (`scripts/skill-case-notes.sh`, wired on PostToolUse `Skill` and UserPromptSubmit).

## Scope
A Codex hook prints a token at skill load; ask the model whether it sees it. Positive control: the same token from `SessionStart`, known to reach the model. Pass: wire Codex to `scripts/skill-case-notes.sh` (adapters/codex/hooks.json). Fail: record it; Codex falls back to a step 0 in the skill (note § 3.5).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Probe result and its positive control recorded on 1394 and here
- [ ] Codex wired, or the fallback named with its reason

## Imagine (raid 1f0534)
- Premise holds: no Codex wiring for skill-case-notes on main. Codex has no Skill tool, so "skill load" is a shell read of `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`: probe whatever hook event Codex fires around that read (PostToolUse on shell, if offered), with the SessionStart positive control.
- Spend: a few `codex exec` calls, authorized by the session's model-service clause.
- Shares `scripts/skill-case-notes.sh` with 1405: change the script only additively (a new payload shape), never its Claude paths.

## Feasibility (raid 1f0534)
- WARN. `~/.codex/hooks.json` is a symlink into the checkout: merging a hooks.json change changes the host. Codex hook trust is hash-recorded (adapters/README.md § dirty-reset guard): probe in a throwaway CODEX_HOME whether 0.166.0 trusts per entry or per file before wiring; a whole-file distrust would silently drop the destructive-bash guard.
- Codex invokes skills as `$name`, not `/name`: the `"prompt":"/` pre-filter in scripts/skill-case-notes.sh:17-19 drops them.
- Record probe results on this ticket only; the orchestrator copies them to 1394 (avoids log conflicts with 1405).
